ed source pairings are labelled. Level bands are planning guidance, not entrance requirements. Blizzard listed 30+ when opening this dungeon; that is not a verified equip-level rule.",ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={},t={},no={S[39],S[41],S[31]}}},{n="Zul'Farrak",lr="44–54",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Maraudon",lr="46–55",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Alcaz Prison",lr="48–53",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar",lr="50–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Blackrock Depths",lr="52–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Dire Maul",lr="54–60",st=S[191],no="Not yet confirmed for this beta loot guide. We do not have confirmed dungeon-drop data. Wings: East 54–60, North and West 56–60.",ba=false},{n="Lower Blackrock Spire",lr="55–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Blackmaw Hold",lr="55–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Scholomance",lr="58–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Stratholme",lr="58–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Shaper’s Terrace",lr="58–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false},{n="Upper Blackrock Spire",lr="59–60",st=S[191],no=S[34],ba=false}},professions={{n="Tailoring",b="Cloth armor for every level, with Forever healing, spell damage and Shadow lines, plus bags. The best leveling profession for Priests.",cv="The best pieces bind on pickup, so you must craft them yourself. Pairs naturally with Enchanting."},{n="Enchanting",b="Your own wands: Novice’s Practice Wand (1), Lesser Magic Wand (5), Greater Magic Wand (13), and later Mystic, Nether, Dreambough and Eternal wands up to Torch of Light at 60. Also Wizard and Mana Oils, gear enchants and disenchanting.",cv="Others can buy the early wands without the profession. Avoid expensive enchants on temporary gear."},{n="Alchemy",b="Mana potions, Intellect, Wisdom and spell damage elixirs, and protection potions. Dyes for other professions sell well.",cv="Ordinary healing potions are First Aid crafts in Forever; discolored Alchemy potions have a different effect."},{n="Herbalism",b="Herbs for Alchemy, or income if you sell them.",cv="Gathering only; no direct combat bonus."},{n="Engineering",b="Explosives and unique trinkets such as Major Recombobulator, Gyrofreeze Ice Reflector and Gnomish Poultryizer. Strongest for Gnome Priests and PvP; Pairs well with Alchemy for raiders.",cv="Pairs with Mining. Guns and scopes are not Priest upgrades."},{n="Mining",b="Ore and stone for Engineering, and income from bars.",cv="Melee attack power from a camp effect is not spell power."},{n="Skinning",b="Leather, hides and scales from beasts; easy early income for training costs.",cv="It does not make leather armor wearable by a Priest."},{n="Cooking",b="Food, drink and campfires; buff food adds stats and extra experience from kills while leveling.",cv="Priests cannot conjure water, so bought or cooked drinks cover recovery between pulls."},{n="First Aid",b="Bandages, normal healing potions and condition-removal items.",cv="Your heals are usually faster than bandages; damage interrupts bandaging."},{n="Fishing",b="Fish for Cooking, including buff-food ingredients.",cv="No guaranteed income is implied."}},gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Dungeon quests whose Priest-usable rewards are recorded in the Forever database, including Gravestone Scepter and the other wand rewards. Quest rewards carry no level requirement of their own, so each tooltip shows the quest level and the level you can pick the quest up from where it is known. Sorted by quest level; check faction before planning a route.",keys={"priest-133","priest-134","priest-137","priest-107","priest-108","priest-103","priest-50","priest-104","priest-144","priest-142","priest-120","priest-143","priest-139","priest-145","priest-121","priest-122","priest-5","priest-61","priest-27","priest-60","priest-59","priest-28","priest-43","priest-146","priest-42","priest-69","priest-12","priest-13","priest-70","priest-71","priest-38","priest-14","priest-126","priest-127","priest-6","priest-7","priest-128","priest-10","pries